<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mattium</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mattium was the chief settlement of the Chatti, a Germanic people of what is now northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> records that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanicus">Germanicus</a> burned it in 15 CE during his campaigns across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> never brought the Chatti under lasting control. Its site is uncertain, though it is often sought near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fritzlar">Fritzlar</a> or Gudensberg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mattium.jpg" alt="Mattium" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kmhkmh · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mattium2.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
